==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Compound of {{com|en|tax|haven}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[jurisdiction]] that [[levy|levies]] low tax rates on certain economic activities, especially to attract wealthy individuals and ([[foreign]]) [[business]]es.
#* '''2013''', Simon Jenkins, ''Gibraltar and the Falklands deny the logic of history'' (in ''The Guardian'', 14 August 2013)[http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/aug/14/gibraltar-falklands-deny-logic-history]
#*: Such colonies claim to be "more British than the British", except that they pay no UK tax and act as '''tax havens''' for funds from Britain. Gibraltar has made a particular specialism of internet gambling.

